.Dd September 16, 2026
.Dt NDI_GET_BUS_STATE 9F
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ndi_get_bus_state ,
.Nm ndi_set_bus_state
.Nd get and set the software state of a bus
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/sunndi.h
.Ft "int"
.Fo ndi_get_bus_state
.Fa "dev_info_t *dip"
.Fa "uint_t *rstate"
.Fc
.Ft "int"
.Fo ndi_set_bus_state
.Fa "dev_info_t *dip"
.Fa "uint_t state"
.Fc
.Sh INTERFACE LEVEL
illumos specific
.Pq Consolidation Private .
.Sh PARAMETERS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Va dip
Valid bus nexus device node.
.It Va rstate
Address of a \fBuint_t\fP in kernel memory receiving the state.
.It Va state
One of \fBBUS_ACTIVE\fP, \fBBUS_QUIESCED\fP, or \fBBUS_SHUTDOWN\fP.
.El
.Sh DESCRIPTION
\fBndi_get_bus_state()\fP stores the nexus's recorded bus state in \fB*rstate\fP.
It returns \fBBUS_QUIESCED\fP when quiesced, otherwise \fBBUS_SHUTDOWN\fP when
marked down, and otherwise \fBBUS_ACTIVE\fP.
The node must have a bus operations vector.
.Pp
\fBndi_set_bus_state()\fP updates the software state to \fBstate\fP.
\fBBUS_QUIESCED\fP sets the quiesced indication.
\fBBUS_SHUTDOWN\fP sets the down indication.
\fBBUS_ACTIVE\fP clears both indications.
If the down and quiesced indications are both present, the getter reports
\fBBUS_QUIESCED\fP.
The functions serialize access to the state internally.
.Pp
Setting this state does not itself stop I/O, power down hardware, detach
children, or invoke bus reset operations.
The nexus must perform the corresponding bus-specific action and record its
result with these functions.
.Sh CONTEXT
These functions may be called from user, kernel, or low-level interrupt
context while the node and its operations vector remain valid.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
These functions return \fBNDI_SUCCESS\fP on success and \fBNDI_FAILURE\fP for
invalid arguments, an unsupported state, or a node without bus operations
when querying state.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ndi_devctl_ioctl 9F ,
.Xr sunndi 9F
